  "changes": [
    "The resource block header derives its 4,544-byte length from labels and records master-pointer offset $7C. The PACK header retains resource ID 4 and version 2.",
    "FPFORMAC is 1; FPFORDEB and FPFORLISA are 0. ROMRSRC remains 0, as in the released driver. Conditional assembly therefore selects the same arithmetic and exception-handling paths as the ROM.",
    "PCOK is 1 to select the original source alternatives that explicitly name the program counter. This changes assembler syntax while retaining the ROM addressing mode.",
    "The zero-valued FOADD push at $41ED5A uses CLR.W -(SP) to reproduce the ROM encoding. The released MOVE.W #FOADD,-(SP) has the same stack value but occupies two more bytes with this assembler.",
    "A NOP at $41F0C6 restores two bytes immediately before BD9. The April 1991 history says that an extraneous branch was removed. That entry is consistent with an earlier assembler replacing a branch to the next instruction with NOP, but the lost source spelling remains uncertain.",
    "The original arithmetic bodies and numeric tables remain in FPCtrl.a, FPOps.a, and FPBD.a. Only the zero push and restored NOP change their active computational statements.",
    "Required SANEMacs and ToolUtils equates retain their original definitions and comments. The StandardEqu load, unused SANEMacs include, listing controls, and later build-wrapper history are omitted. Original authorship, copyright, and routine histories remain.",
    "The unprefixed DELETED annotation in FPCtrl.a gains a semicolon so it remains a comment. Decimal constants with leading zeros retain their original spelling; the shared translator now preserves their decimal values."
  ],
